fix: stop the activity bar claiming an update on a fresh install

The badge is cleared by writing a value first and the clear behind it,
because VS Code drops a clear that matches the cached badge on a view
rebuilt after being hidden. That priming write ran on the first view of
all, where there was no stale count to clear - so the value landed and
the clear behind it was the no-op instead.

Split the one flag in two: whether this view object has been written to,
and whether the icon is actually showing a count. The priming write now
needs both.
